From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rzg2l-cru: set AXI burst length to fix 4K RAW12
 per-line truncation

On RZ/V2N, 4K RAW12 capture writes only ~58% of each line to memory (the
rest is zeros) - the original "RAW12 truncated to ~55% per line" bug.
Everything upstream (sensor, CSI-2, CRU-IP pads) is correct 3840x2160;
the CRU DMA simply stops mid-line.

Root cause: rzg2l_cru_initialize_axi() never programs AMnAXIATTR, so the
CRU AXI master uses its reset (short) burst length and cannot drain the
line FIFO fast enough at high pixel rates. The FIFO overflows partway
through each line and the tail is lost.

Set AMnAXIATTR.AXILEN to the maximum (0xf), the recommended setting - the
same write the RZ AI-SDK CRU driver (meta-rz-imx415) performs. With this,
4K RAW12 lines are captured in full.

Signed-off-by: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-cru-regs.h b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-cru-regs.h
index bb25813281bb..a5744eed0e9b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-cru-regs.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-cru-regs.h
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@
 #define AMnIS_IS_MASK			GENMASK(14, 7)
 #define AMnIS_IS(x)			((x) << 7)
 
+#define AMnAXIATTR_AXILEN		GENMASK(3, 0)
+
 #define AMnAXISTP_AXI_STOP		BIT(0)
 
 #define AMnAXISTPACK_AXI_STOP_ACK	BIT(0)
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c
index cbf92303a5e1..0e20d6fcb136 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c
@@ -407,6 +407,16 @@ static void rzg2l_cru_initialize_axi(struct rzg2l_cru_dev *cru)
 		stride /= RZG2L_CRU_STRIDE_ALIGN;
 		amnis = rzg2l_cru_read(cru, AMnIS) & ~AMnIS_IS_MASK;
 		rzg2l_cru_write(cru, AMnIS, amnis | AMnIS_IS(stride));
+
+		/*
+		 * Set the AXI master burst length to the maximum (recommended)
+		 * so the CRU can drain its line FIFO fast enough. Without this
+		 * the FIFO overflows mid-line at high pixel rates (e.g. 4K
+		 * RAW12) and each line is truncated to ~58%. Matches the RZ
+		 * AI-SDK CRU driver.
+		 */
+		amnis = rzg2l_cru_read(cru, AMnAXIATTR) & ~AMnAXIATTR_AXILEN;
+		rzg2l_cru_write(cru, AMnAXIATTR, amnis | 0xf);
 	}
 }
 
